# Copy to .env.local for development. Do not commit .env.local.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUDIT_LOG_PATH — REQUIRED BEFORE REAL TRAFFIC
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where audit records are written. Every generated letter, report and referral
# package writes one, recording the compliance tier, disclaimer version and
# analysis basis active at that moment. The point of the record is to stay
# answerable about an artefact months after it went out.
#
# Unset, the app falls back to ./.audit/sends.jsonl and warns on screen. That is
# fine locally and is NOT a production configuration, for a reason that is easy
# to miss: on a serverless host (Vercel, Lambda, Cloud Run) the filesystem is
# EPHEMERAL. Writes succeed, the app reports no error, and every record is gone
# at the next cold start. A silent total loss is the worst possible failure for
# this particular file.
#
# On a VM or container with a mounted volume, point this at that volume.
# On a serverless host, a file path is not sufficient at all — replace the
# adapter in src/lib/compliance/audit-store.ts with a database-backed one. The
# AuditStore interface exists so that is a drop-in.
#
AUDIT_LOG_PATH=./.audit/sends.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY — not needed while the product is free
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Commerce is disabled in code (src/lib/compliance/commerce-mode.ts) pending
# counsel review, so no checkout session can be created and this key is unused.
# It is listed here so nobody concludes it was forgotten.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENABLE_OPERATOR_PAGES — LEAVE UNSET ON ANY PUBLIC HOST
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Opens /readiness, which is an operator tool and not part of the product.
#
# That page publishes the server's filesystem paths, every open compliance gap
# in full, and every accepted-risk rationale with its owner and date —
# including that Track 1 currently operates without a counsel opinion, in the
# product's own words. All of it is written down deliberately; none of it is
# written down for publication at a guessable URL.
#
# Unset, /readiness returns 404 in production. That is the correct state. It is
# open automatically in development, because a local server is already your own
# machine.
#
# Must equal exactly "1". The same information is available by running the test
# suite, without serving it to anyone.
#
# ENABLE_OPERATOR_PAGES=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — set it on the deployed host
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public origin, e.g. https://easement.example.com. Used for the canonical
# metadata base and for the Sitemap: line in robots.txt.
#
# Unset, it falls back to http://localhost:3000. That is deliberately an
# obviously-wrong value rather than a guessed domain: a wrong absolute URL in a
# canonical tag points crawlers at somebody else's site and asks them to treat
# it as authoritative, which is worse than a useless one.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-host.example.com
